ame":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:41:25-07:00","id":971424,"title":"","content":"Made it easy to do cross overs....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:21:10-07:00","id":971522,"title":"","content":"It also added options for playing (comparatively) good Technocrats, as they had some internal corruption to fight. Granted, there was already a whole lot of internal corruption, but this adds to it. Because of course, if the Union at large knew about what SPD was really doing, they would never stand for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:35:11-07:00","id":971807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971405#post971405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WoD, everyone is a monster. Introducing the SPD to &quot;demonize&quot; the Technos is like adding water to the ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think so - Pentex connection is not only significantly damaging besmirching morality of the Technocracy, but also undermining and tainting their dedication to cause and ideal, purity of doctrine and ideology as well as making idiotic imbeciles of them. All in all, this contrived, unnatural Pentex connection must be deliberate, thoughtful and connotative decision of the White Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:06:43-07:00","id":971817,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think that it makes sense for the Technocracy and Pentex to exist in the same universe. I existence of one undermines the importance of the other. That is the downside of crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:40:10-07:00","id":971856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971807#post971807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex connection is not only significantly damaging besmirching morality of the Technocracy, but also undermining and tainting their dedication to cause and ideal, purity of doctrine and ideology</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the entire point of the Technocracy. Their ideals are subordinate to their interests, at least at an institutional level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as well as making idiotic imbeciles of them. </div> </div> </div>They kinda are idiots, or at least they're arrogant enough to think they can always come out on top. Bear in mind, the Syndicate don't generally have Dimensional Science, hardly anyone does in the Technocracy outside the VE. It's not that big a stretch for a small group of Syndicate members to get involved with Pentex, not really understanding what they're doing until it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:50:46-07:00","id":971861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971807#post971807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think so - Pentex connection is not only significantly damaging besmirching morality of the Technocracy, but also undermining and tainting their dedication to cause and ideal, purity of doctrine and ideology as well as making idiotic imbeciles of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeahhh...how does that contradict my post?<br /> undermining their dedication doesn't mean they're demonizing them. Technocracy, like everyone else, is already demonized, with or without Pentex.<br /> Nobody's perfect, everyone is arrogantly rotten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All in all, this contrived, unnatural Pentex connection must be deliberate, thoughtful and connotative decision of the White Wolf. </div> </div> </div>Yes, like everything else in the game...(it's a white wolf fiction, remember?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Technos are not the only ones. Most WoD factions have &quot;bad apples&quot; that spoil their image. That sort of plot element is introduced to prevent players from losing themselves in power fantasies or idolizing their faction too much.<br /> <br /> If technocracy (or anything else) was flawless, it wouldn't be called World of Darkness but World of my awesome Heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971817#post971817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't think that it makes sense for the Technocracy and Pentex to exist in the same universe. I existence of one undermines the importance of the other. That is the downside of crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we also remove demons from VtM, because it undermines the Sabbat? should we remove kuei-jin because it mocks the Anarchs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T05:16:13-07:00","id":971888,"title":"","content":"I'd say SPD is here to underline the danger of being manipulated and made pawns, even as seemingly safe and knowledgeable Mages. I see it definitely as a comment on the amorality and narrowmindedness of the Syndicate. The Arete 7 Manager (or is he a Chairman?) from first Syndicate Convention Book gives support and safe haven to a group of Fomori led by a Black Spiral, because he is under the impression that he controls them cause they work as his casino security. As long as the money flows and the muscle is top-notch, it's all fine, isn't it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971807#post971807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think so - Pentex connection is not only significantly damaging besmirching morality of the Technocracy, but also undermining and tainting their dedication to cause and ideal, purity of doctrine and ideology as well as making idiotic imbeciles of them. All in all, this contrived, unnatural Pentex connection must be deliberate, thoughtful and connotative decision of the White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why call it contrived, and that it makes Technocracy look like imbeciles? Even disregarding Nephandi, Pentex still has Enticers (who have social attributes of 6 and two more powers for seduction), psychic Fomori, cultists with powers, and Black Spirals. As well as being cunning, devoted and looking for the long game.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Syndicate accepting enchanced muscle in the form of Fomori makes a certain amount sense - it made them less dependent on Iteration-X support or Progenitor creations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-18-2016, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:16:50-07:00","id":971933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971888#post971888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, the Syndicate accepting enchanced muscle in the form of Fomori makes a certain amount sense - it made them less dependent on Iteration-X support or Progenitor creations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And,even more important, Fomori are cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:03:51-07:00","id":971952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971817#post971817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't think that it makes sense for the Technocracy and Pentex to exist in the same universe. I existence of one undermines the importance of the other. That is the downside of crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to come to some concessions if you want a World of Crossover-y Darkness. If you can't encompass them within the constraints of your visions of the game, of course the overlaps don't work.<br /> <br /> If Pentex is as all-encompassing evil as presented in Werewolf, the the point that it informs, invents, subverts and encompasses all corporate culture, there isn't room for the Syndicate. Or only for a very small Syndicate (as part of a very small Union as part of a very small overall number of mages who have a very small overall effect on a world going straight down to Wyrm-ish Hell). <br /> <br /> If in your Mage game, the Syndicate is in absolute control of the world economy, it HAS to know about Pentex and it would be idiocy to be clueless about their RD aspects, including stuff that screams &quot;NEPHANDI!&quot; in blood-colored neon. Especially considering that Pentex is so obviously and openly involved in so many high-profile aspects of commerce. The entire Syndicate would know about it, not just SPD and SPD would have a very hard time keeping a secret relationship very secret, and, though it's entirely possible, coming up with a reason why the Syndicate is not doing it's job and leaving a significant portion of the world's economy in the hands of RD's in, in terms of long term cost-benefit analysis, a remarkably BAD idea. Said reasons (the whole Technephandi thing &lt;ick&gt;, Hubris as described above... &quot;We can control them. They can be controlled...&quot;, etc.) do make enough sense in context of Mage to work better than seeing it through Werewolf goggles.<br /> <br /> Probably the best route to take in a crossover world is that there is a whole lot of mis-perception and propaganda going on. The Syndicate no more controls the economy than Pentex does. The world is big enough that both can exist and brush up against one another, but, if each is focused elsewhere, convinced of it's own supremacy in its area, etc. they effectively co-exist. Kinda like the Camarilla and Union think they both control pretty much everything (except that which they don't and is on the slate for future hegemony) Sure, the Syndicate has a big lever by which to make changes and can be the tail that wags the dog, but a lot of that power is invested in advancing the status quo. Pentex has Maeljin Incarnae keeping it on the down low when the Syndicate's plan-scopers are doing their worldwide Entropy/Primal Utility/Correspondence/Time Procedures to massage commerce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:44:03-07:00","id":971975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971952#post971952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to come to some concessions if you want a World of Crossover-y Darkness. If you can't encompass them within the constraints of your visions of the game, of course the overlaps don't work.<br /> <br /> If Pentex is as all-encompassing evil as presented in Werewolf, the the point that it informs, invents, subverts and encompasses all corporate culture, there isn't room for the Syndicate. Or only for a very small Syndicate (as part of a very small Union as part of a very small overall number of mages who have a very small overall effect on a world going straight down to Wyrm-ish Hell).<br /> <br /> If in your Mage game, the Syndicate is in absolute control of the world economy, it HAS to know about Pentex and it would be idiocy to be clueless about their RD aspects, including stuff that screams &quot;NEPHANDI!&quot; in blood-colored neon. Especially considering that Pentex is so obviously and openly involved in so many high-profile aspects of commerce. The entire Syndicate would know about it, not just SPD and SPD would have a very hard time keeping a secret relationship very secret, and, though it's entirely possible, coming up with a reason why the Syndicate is not doing it's job and leaving a significant portion of the world's economy in the hands of RD's in, in terms of long term cost-benefit analysis, a remarkably BAD idea. Said reasons (the whole Technephandi thing &lt;ick&gt;, Hubris as described above... &quot;We can control them. They can be controlled...&quot;, etc.) do make enough sense in context of Mage to work better than seeing it through Werewolf goggles.<br /> <br /> Probably the best route to take in a crossover world is that there is a whole lot of mis-perception and propaganda going on. The Syndicate no more controls the economy than Pentex does. The world is big enough that both can exist and brush up against one another, but, if each is focused elsewhere, convinced of it's own supremacy in its area, etc. they effectively co-exist. Kinda like the Camarilla and Union think they both control pretty much everything (except that which they don't and is on the slate for future hegemony) Sure, the Syndicate has a big lever by which to make changes and can be the tail that wags the dog, but a lot of that power is invested in advancing the status quo. Pentex has Maeljin Incarnae keeping it on the down low when the Syndicate's plan-scopers are doing their worldwide Entropy/Primal Utility/Correspondence/Time Procedures to massage commerce.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in the your vision of crossover, each major factions control roughly what percentage of the world economy, politics and culture? Chiefly the Union, the Camarilla and the Pentex, three of the most powerful movers-and-shakers-on the Earth? (in their respective setting, of course, and in case of the Union, the very Universe itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-18-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:17:33-07:00","id":971991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971861#post971861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we also remove demons from VtM, because it undermines the Sabbat? should we remove kuei-jin because it mocks the Anarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that demons in V:tM undermine the themes and importance of the Sabbat, the influence of Infernalism has been a problem in the Sabbat since the first Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat. I wouldn't want to bring in too much D:tF stuff into V:tM though, because the nature of the demons are quite different and it could distract from the themes in vampire. <br /> <br /> I'm not even sure what you mean about the Kuei-Jin mocking the Anarchs, but personally I probably would avoid bring Kuei-Jin into a vampire game as I think that it negatively affects the flavor of a standard vampire game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971952#post971952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to come to some concessions if you want a World of Crossover-y Darkness. If you can't encompass them within the constraints of your visions of the game, of course the overlaps don't work.<br /> <br /> If Pentex is as all-encompassing evil as presented in Werewolf, the the point that it informs, invents, subverts and encompasses all corporate culture, there isn't room for the Syndicate. Or only for a very small Syndicate (as part of a very small Union as part of a very small overall number of mages who have a very small overall effect on a world going straight down to Wyrm-ish Hell). <br /> <br /> If in your Mage game, the Syndicate is in absolute control of the world economy, it HAS to know about Pentex and it would be idiocy to be clueless about their RD aspects, including stuff that screams &amp;quot;NEPHANDI!&amp;quot; in blood-colored neon. Especially considering that Pentex is so obviously and openly involved in so many high-profile aspects of commerce. The entire Syndicate would know about it, not just SPD and SPD would have a very hard time keeping a secret relationship very secret, and, though it's entirely possible, coming up with a reason why the Syndicate is not doing it's job and leaving a significant portion of the world's economy in the hands of RD's in, in terms of long term cost-benefit analysis, a remarkably BAD idea. Said reasons (the whole Technephandi thing &lt;ick&gt;, Hubris as described above... &amp;quot;We can control them. They can be controlled...&amp;quot;, etc.) do make enough sense in context of Mage to work better than seeing it through Werewolf goggles.<br /> <br /> Probably the best route to take in a crossover world is that there is a whole lot of mis-perception and propaganda going on. The Syndicate no more controls the economy than Pentex does. The world is big enough that both can exist and brush up against one another, but, if each is focused elsewhere, convinced of it's own supremacy in its area, etc. they effectively co-exist. Kinda like the Camarilla and Union think they both control pretty much everything (except that which they don't and is on the slate for future hegemony) Sure, the Syndicate has a big lever by which to make changes and can be the tail that wags the dog, but a lot of that power is invested in advancing the status quo. Pentex has Maeljin Incarnae keeping it on the down low when the Syndicate's plan-scopers are doing their worldwide Entropy/Primal Utility/Correspondence/Time Procedures to massage commerce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that if you're going to have a crossover, it might be best not to answer the big questions. Let everything be mysterious, even out of character. The characters aren't going to know how much respective power Pentex has in comparison to the Syndicate and so players don't have to know either. In fact, the ST doesn't even have to know. <br /> <br /> In most cases, I prefer non-crossover single game settings because how the games kind of step on each others' thematic toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:47:37-07:00","id":972009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971991#post971991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that demons in V:tM undermine the themes and importance of the Sabbat, the influence of Infernalism has been a problem in the Sabbat since the first Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat. I wouldn't want to bring in too much D:tF stuff into V:tM though, because the nature of the demons are quite different and it could distract from the themes in vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure what you mean about the Kuei-Jin mocking the Anarchs, but personally I probably would avoid bring Kuei-Jin into a vampire game as I think that it negatively affects the flavor of a standard vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, obviously, you don't know the story. The Pentex/Technocracy problem came late in the game. The Infernalist/Sabbat problem also came late.<br /> In the first portrayals of the Sabbat/Technocracy (before their respective sourcebooks), both sounded quite flawless. And, though they were considered the villains, they both looked like the perfect winning team.<br /> <br /> When Sabbat was made to be a playable DnD faction (in the first guide), they changed that. They introduced Demons as their main problem as well as Lupines and Vicissitude Umbral disease (among other crossover things). Then, in Revised, they changed it once more and made the Sabbat less DnD (Demons are still a problem, just not the central problem).<br /> <br /> It was the same for the Technos, when they made it a playable faction, they had to fix the &quot;flawless&quot; aspect of the Union (either with Pentex or something else).<br /> <br /> As for the Anarch/kuei-jin problem. The main reason Anarchs in San Fransisco were (almost) obliterated and put down was because one of their Leaders surrendered to the Kuei-Jin (I'm surprised you didn't even know that). Kuei-Jin have been playing them fools ever since.<br /> <br /> There are other examples as well: Bamboo Princes with Tremere/Brujah, Genji with Sabbat...the pattern repeats itself, always for the same purpose: adding some flaws to the factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-18-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:58:20-07:00","id":972016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972009#post972009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, obviously, you don't know the story. The Pentex/Technocracy problem came late in the game. The Infernalist/Sabbat problem also came late.<br /> In the first portrayals of the Sabbat/Technocracy (before their respective sourcebooks), both sounded quite flawless. And, though they were considered the villains, they both looked like the perfect winning team.<br /> <br /> When Sabbat was made to be a playable DnD faction (in the first guide), they changed that. They introduced Demons as their main problem as well as Lupines and Vicissitude Umbral disease (among other crossover things). Then, in Revised, they changed it once more and made the Sabbat less DnD (Demons are still a problem, just not the central problem).<br /> <br /> It was the same for the Technos, when they made it a playable faction, they had to fix the &quot;flawless&quot; aspect of the Union (either with Pentex or something else).<br /> <br /> As for the Anarch/kuei-jin problem. The main reason Anarchs in San Fransisco were (almost) obliterated and put down was because one of their Leaders surrendered to the Kuei-Jin (I'm surprised you didn't even know that). Kuei-Jin have been playing them fools ever since.<br /> <br /> There are other examples as well: Bamboo Princes with Tremere/Brujah, Genji with Sabbat...the pattern repeats itself, always for the same purpose: adding some flaws to the factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, except the Black Hand and the Pentex.<br /> <br /> Both of them are perfect. A little <i>too </i>perfect, with absolute zero of debilitating, outside-introduced flaws or dark secrets.<br /> <br /> And then, there is so <i>much </i>pristine, immaculate Camarilla...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-18-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:21:32-07:00","id":972028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972016#post972016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, except the Black Hand and the Pentex.<br /> <br /> Both of them are perfect. A little <i>too </i>perfect, with absolute zero of debilitating, outside-introduced flaws or dark secrets.<br /> <br /> And then, there is so <i>much </i>pristine, immaculate Camarilla...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly true.<br /> <br /> Though, the Black Hand were pretty much put as the big losers in Revised. Maybe they plan to do the same for Pentex and the Cam in the new edition (the cam is just too damn powerful, too perfect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-18-2016, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:55:58-07:00","id":972142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972016#post972016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then, there is so <i>much </i>pristine, immaculate Camarilla...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972028#post972028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (the cam is just too damn powerful, too perfect).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little curious what you mean here. The Camarilla is anything but pristine, immaculate, or perfect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:04:39-07:00","id":972146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972016#post972016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, except the Black Hand and the Pentex.<br /> <br /> Both of them are perfect. A little <i>too </i>perfect, with absolute zero of debilitating, outside-introduced flaws or dark secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Book of the Wyrm disagrees on the latter. It has no small amount of internal rivalries, rivalries with other heads of the Hydra, or social engineering vulnerabilities, Garou just hail from a culture where you get more recognition from gutting a giant monster than when you sweet-talk a mortal dupe of the enemy into revealing its dirty laundry. You want a Fera that values Cunning Renown to get on the fast track doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:17:27-07:00","id":972155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972146#post972146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 Book of the Wyrm disagrees on the latter. It has no small amount of internal rivalries, rivalries with other heads of the Hydra, or social engineering vulnerabilities</div> </div> </div> </div>So? their image remains untouched, untainted. They are who they are.<br /> <br /> Sabbat have internal conflicts and infighting, but each rival serves the Sabbat. Infernalists, though are a cancer to their ideals and goals (as well as Alamut servants and BH con men), just like SPD is a cancer to Techno ideals/goals, just like Kuei-Jin are cancer to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> But Pentex is...pure Pentex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm a little curious what you mean here. The Camarilla is anything but pristine, immaculate, or perfect. </div> </div> </div>They're pragmatic aristocrat snobs securing their long term interests. Period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:23:09-07:00","id":972159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972146#post972146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 Book of the Wyrm disagrees on the latter. It has no small amount of internal rivalries, rivalries with other heads of the Hydra, or social engineering vulnerabilities, Garou just hail from a culture where you get more recognition from gutting a giant monster than when you sweet-talk a mortal dupe of the enemy into revealing its dirty laundry. You want a Fera that values Cunning Renown to get on the fast track doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already know that. That is the reason why I have explicitly stated &quot;outside-introduced&quot;. Internal rivalries are precisely what expected from excessively competitive, selfish and morally bankrupt organizations like the Pentex. That is just a natural development. Their divisive weakness is inevitable outgrowth from corrupt, rotten field. What I means is, the Hydra does not hide any skeleton in the closet nor embedded automatic kill switch.<br /> <br /> Camarilla is just same. So the organization itself is pristine and immaculate with no outside-introduced weak points, even though the organization's honey-bucketed morality is anything but.<br /> <br /> A long story short, the Pentex and the Camarilla does not have its own Special Projects Division or suchlike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:24:08-07:00","id":972161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972142#post972142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little curious what you mean here. The Camarilla is anything but pristine, immaculate, or perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my comment above. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:43:07-07:00","id":972178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972159#post972159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already know that. That is the reason why I have explicitly stated &quot;outside-introduced&quot;. Internal rivalries are precisely what expected from excessively competitive, selfish and morally bankrupt organizations like the Pentex. That is just a natural development. Their divisive weakness is inevitable outgrowth from corrupt, rotten field. What I means is, the Hydra does not hide any skeleton in the closet or kill switch.<br /> <br /> Camarilla is just same. So the organization itself is pristine and immaculate with no outside-introduced weak points, even though the organization's honey-bucketed morality is anything but.<br /> <br /> A long story short, the Pentex and the Camarilla does not have its own Special Projects Division or suchlike.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of difficult to corrupt the corrupted. You may be looking for an equivalence that doesn't really exist; Pentex is its own SPD, instead of having a distinct turncoat division, for example. It's such a massive, bloated bureaucracy, you could theoretically hide behind some position in one of the subsidiaries while hurting the company, and there would be a huge blind spot in which to conceal yourself for a good long while. Actually looking into such problems would cost the companies a large amount of time, labor, and money, so it'd be possible to shift around which one you're using as a cover, if you were clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:13:12-07:00","id":972188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection#post971380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the White Wolf had decided to introduce SPD so thoroughly corrupted by their underhanded dealing with the Pentex? Simply to demonize the amoral capitalistic Syndicate and make fun of the foolish authoritarian Technocracy? Or is it a backfired attempt to provide an intriguing play option? Would the M20 revise things going background a little differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>My theory:<br /> <br /> &quot;Well this one group is a corporation and a villain, and this other group has corporations and is a villain, so wouldn't it be neat if we could <i>combine</i> them?&quot;<br /> -Someone on White Wolf's writing staff while stoned, maybe<br /> <br /> And then it snowballed from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:44:05-07:00","id":972203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972159#post972159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already know that. That is the reason why I have explicitly stated &quot;outside-introduced&quot;. Internal rivalries are precisely what expected from excessively competitive, selfish and morally bankrupt organizations like the Pentex. That is just a natural development. Their divisive weakness is inevitable outgrowth from corrupt, rotten field. What I means is, the Hydra does not hide any skeleton in the closet nor embedded automatic kill switch.<br /> <br /> Camarilla is just same. So the organization itself is pristine and immaculate with no outside-introduced weak points, even though the organization's honey-bucketed morality is anything but.<br /> <br /> A long story short, the Pentex and the Camarilla does not have its own Special Projects Division or suchlike.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972155#post972155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're pragmatic aristocrat snobs securing their long term interests. Period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not really sure what the point is you're trying to make.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:17:30-07:00","id":972300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=971975#post971975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the your vision of crossover, each major factions control roughly what percentage of the world economy, politics and culture? Chiefly the Union, the Camarilla and the Pentex, three of the most powerful movers-and-shakers-on the Earth? (in their respective setting, of course, and in case of the Union, the very Universe itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a question that can really be answered. What percentage of the world economy is the E.U. commerce? Sure, we can answer that. But can be compare it with, say the interrelated amounts in the various commodities exchanges? With the illegal antiquities market generated by ISIL? With venture capitalists associated with the technological or biomedical industry? Vs. the amount of loans given out by independant banks in the US? Those are on completely different vectors. They interrelated. They cross over. They exist at different levels and are viewed via different perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:24:04-07:00","id":972302,"title":"","content":"SPD was a thing in Pentex for the longest time. If they weren't going to be from the Syndicate then they would just be random Nephandi, and Sorcerers. So it really works with them being Syndicate since well they are the Corporate mad scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:37:37-07:00","id":972381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972203#post972203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not really sure what the point is you're trying to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you really not comprehend the words, or simply feigning ignorance?<br /> <br /> Let me ask you straightforward: how many skeletons in the closet t<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">he Camarilla conceal except their </span></span></span>na\u00efve <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">lying about A</span></span></span>ntediluvian<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">? Would their dirty little secrets </span></span></span>shake the very foundation of the institution if revealed in the daylight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-19-2016, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:00:00-07:00","id":972385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972381#post972381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really not comprehend the words, or simply feigning ignorance?<br /> <br /> Let me ask you straightforward: how many skeletons in the closet t<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">he Camarilla conceal except their </span></span></span>na\u00efve <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">lying about A</span></span></span>ntediluvian<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">? Would their dirty little secrets </span></span></span>shake the very foundation of the institution if revealed in the daylight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the Inner Council aren't as cohesive as the Conventions, they are extremely powerful Methuselahs and Elders but yeah individually their secrets are hella bad. Tremere do naughty things in secret, for one they didn't wipe clean the Gargoyle experiments like they claim. A single Ventrue has an island of Revenants that secretly are the product of infernal legacies. Diablerie and End time dealings about. They are all about covering up their silly and wicked secrets. Hell friggin Hardstadt isn't even friggin Hardstadt he is the Childe of Hardstadt! Karsh is friggin Jaalan Ajav! Javier had Gangrel leave because he found out the Inner Council knows that the Antes are awakening and are nightmares incarnate but are choosing to ignore it.<br /> <br /> All potentially very fragile...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:25:12-07:00","id":972588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972381#post972381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really not comprehend the words, or simply feigning ignorance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I think pretty much the same thing any time I read your gibberish. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972381#post972381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me ask you straightforward: how many skeletons in the closet the Camarilla conceal except their na\u00efve lying about Antediluvian? Would their dirty little secrets shake the very foundation of the institution if revealed in the daylight?</div> </div> </div> </div>There we go, sense at last! Still not sure how it relates to the original point, but let me take a crack at it. You already touched upon their rejection of Antediluvian mythology, the weaknesses of which are more a product of not being adequately explored in the text. As an extension of that Elder and Antediluvian cults are present beneath the surface of the sect, as are Infernalists and secret Path followers, any of which if exposed would threaten the Camarilla's gilded edifice and compromise what little ideology they profess to have. Somehow I don't think that's what you're looking for though. The Camarilla doesn't really have skeletons in the closet because their skeletons are on the living room couch. You only put them in the closet if you actually have a reason to hide them. The Camarilla only maintains the barest pretense of being a morally upright organization, their foundations are built on power and realpolitik. The only secret that would really shake those foundations is if it turned out they really had no power at all. Certainly the Antediluvian-denial is related to that, but in the end the Camarilla's pyramid scheme nature makes their power and strength (while not at all monolithic) a self-fulfilling prophecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:28:26-07:00","id":972605,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> You are basically proving his point. The Cam has no cancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:46:13-07:00","id":972611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972605#post972605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> You are basically proving his point. The Cam has no cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what you guys mean by &quot;pristine&quot; &quot;immaculate&quot; and &quot;perfect&quot; then sure, I guess I am. The reason the Camarilla doesn't have a cancer though is because the Camarilla <i>is</i> a cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:08:57-07:00","id":972629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972605#post972605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> You are basically proving his point. The Cam has no cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, if we do not take in account the Gangrel Schism, the Inner Circle leaks by Madame Guil,Kemintiri and so on, the whole &quot;we know Ghenna is true and if the young ones find this out we are finished&quot; thing, the &quot;Saulot is sleeping on the Tremere's couch&quot; doomsday button, the fact that Camarilla is losing the war with the Sabbat, the secrets of the Tremere violating the Montmartre Pact with the Nosfe gathering the proofs to oust them,the Malkavian restoriation of Dementation that threatens the Masquerade,the Niktuku problem,the murder of Petrodon, plus the tons of lesser cancer that there is in every single city in the form of Camarilla politics, secrets and plots that goes from Lodin's &quot;I'm Helena's pawn&quot; to Vitel &quot;I'm not even a ventrue!&quot; to Hardestadt &quot;I'm not even me at all!&quot; than yeah, they have no cancer at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-19-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:26:32-07:00","id":972680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972611#post972611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's what you guys mean by &quot;pristine&quot; &quot;immaculate&quot; and &quot;perfect&quot; then sure, I guess I am. The reason the Camarilla doesn't have a cancer though is because the Camarilla <i>is</i> a cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Their founders made it so the organization would be like a sponge that could absorb anything while still remaining a sponge. Or is it the Ivory tower that no matter what hits it, it remains the same?...I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Whatever happens in the Camarilla is just &quot;business as usual&quot;.<br /> <br /> How can an organization be so pragmatic, so neutral, so devoid of any standing or purpose, so...perfect that nothing in existence may shake them?<br /> Hell, even the Infernalists aren't that hollow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972629#post972629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if we do not take in account the...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we sure do not take the Antes (and anything related) into account, because the Antes can destroy the world even by accident.<br /> <br /> What you described is no cancer, it's the Camarilla status quo. Sabbat have similar stuff that constitutes their status quo.<br /> But since the Sabbat and Technos are not so pragmatic, since they wage wars to achieve some &quot;higher purpose&quot;, they had external cancers added to them to undermine their standing and spoil their image. Otherwise they would've been called Heroes.<br /> <br /> Pentex cannot be spoiled (being tainted is their purpose), and the Camarilla has no &quot;higher purpose&quot; to spoil.<br /> <br /> Then, I'm not sure why you're saying the Cam is losing (they're not). But, like I said in my previous posts. The Black Hand, which was just as perfect, ended up losing pretty badly. So, perhaps Camarilla would face a similar fate. If only to snap them out of their convenient pragmatism and force them out of their comfort zones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:48:53-07:00","id":972743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972680#post972680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can an organization be so pragmatic, so neutral, so devoid of any standing or purpose, so...perfect that nothing in existence may shake them?<br /> Hell, even the Infernalists aren't that hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla is far from unassailable, internal fissures are plentiful and external threats abound, they just don't really have any particular &quot;dirty secret&quot; like you seem to want them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:40:54-07:00","id":972780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972743#post972743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is far from unassailable, internal fissures are plentiful and external threats abound, they just don't really have any particular &quot;dirty secret&quot; like you seem to want them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't care about them having dirty secrets. I just find them a bit boring...and too &quot;human&quot;. One thing I liked about Kuei-Jin, is that they all acted as vampires, they all had a higher purpose, regardless of faction. I wish the Camarilla was no different.<br /> <br /> Having dirty secrets is not necessary, it just serves to avoid the &quot;vampion&quot; archetype (because WoD is a game about monsters, not champions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:45:51-07:00","id":972783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972680#post972680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Then, I'm not sure why you're saying the Cam is losing (they're not).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehm...yes they are? It is the whole point of the Revised edition:Sabbat is winning the war, Cammarilla managed to hold only by taking New York, but besides that entire East cost is lost under De Polonia's Crusade, West Coast too to Anarchs and Cathayans, Camarilla in United States is isolated and besieged,and even more the Camarilla is losing the cultural war against the &quot;noddist&quot; as more Ghenna cults rise in the wake of the final nights.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:56:38-07:00","id":972792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972783#post972783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cammarilla managed to hold only by taking New York, but besides that entire East cost is lost under De Polonia's Crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for long. The east coast is held thanks to the false hand, and with the fall of the Tal'mahe'ra, Galbraith's death (their main supporter), Assamite defecting to Ur-Shulgi and the conflict with the Inquisition and Templars. The false hand will soon fall, leaving the east coast in a fragile position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:03:51-07:00","id":972798,"title":"","content":"Nope, the false hand is stable, Jalan-Ajav has taken the reins of it and has pretty much everything under control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE NEW COMMAND<br /> In the Final Nights, Jalan-Aajav, or Aajav-Khan to those<br /> who know him well, stands as the de facto First Seraph of the<br /> Black Hand. Already his leadership has borne significant<br /> challenges, such as the abrupt and unexpected desertion of the<br /> eldest of the Assamite antitribu in the middle of one of the<br /> biggest Sabbat offensives in its history . It was Jalan-Aajav who<br /> initiated an investigation into the nature of the treachery, and<br /> presented his findings to the consistory . His quick response to<br /> the crisis doubtless saved many Assamite members of the Black<br /> Hand from the retribution of their fellow Sabbat over the<br /> betrayal of the Assamite elders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>More recently, Jalan-Aajav has acted to preserve the<br /> Black Hand's internal stability by appointing not three, but<br /> four experienced and qualified dominions to fill the seats of the<br /> missing Seraphim - at least for the duration of the present<br /> uncertaint</b>y . He chose four, rather than three, for political<br /> reasons . First, he can potentially offer the future regent the<br /> opportunity to select which three would keep their title and<br /> position on the council . Second, the competition between the<br /> four juniors on the council will hopefully keep them from<br /> uniting in an alliance against him -Jalan-Aajav will permit<br /> no further thwarting of his vision or his plans for the Black<br /> Hand in these Final Nights . His choices included the Nosferatu<br /> dominion Teresita, a staunch Ultra-Conservative, but also a<br /> resident of Mexico City and a well-respected strategist ; Yazid<br /> Tamari, an emerging leader among the remaining Assamite<br /> antitribu, whose political savvy (and apparent ignorance of his<br /> grandsire Djuhah's secrets) is an asset when dealing with the<br /> consistory ; Banjoko, a Lasombra whose reputation among the<br /> traditional Noddists and even the Inquisition is that of a<br /> conciliator and pragmatist; and finally, the Tzimisce Kazimir<br /> Savostin, an experienced spy, shakar and Noddist scholar -<br /> and a former associate of Izhim ur-Baal, but whose loyalty to the<br /> Hand Jalan-Aajav has declared unassailable .<br /> The acting council has elevated more veteran operatives<br /> to the ranks of the dominions, and redistributed the Black<br /> Hand's membership among the Sabbat packs as needed to fill<br /> the weaknesses the Assamite desertion left in the Hand's eyes<br /> and ears.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even the Regency matter is not a real problem: If thing takes to long, or the right man is not chosen, Jalan-Ajav will have the ultimate word about it , via praetorian coup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE REGENCY QUESTION<br /> The vacant regency is naturally an issue of great concern to<br /> the Black Hand, which owes its exalted position among the<br /> Sabbat to the support of the regent and the consistory. Galbraith<br /> trusted and relied on the Hand to carry out her agenda, and<br /> otherwise left the subsect independent of outside authority -<br /> which is how the Hand liked it . Of the three candidates, the<br /> Lasombra Charles VI seems the most likely to support the<br /> Hand's agenda against the Antediluvians - on the other hand,<br /> he's almost too cozy with the Inquisition, and might not give the<br /> Hand the freedom to pursue its goals as it wants . Venere<br /> Carboni, a Toreador, was one of Galbraith's supporters, and is<br /> likely to continue with her style of leadership - but if these are<br /> indeed the Final Nights, would business as usual mean stability<br /> or stagnation? Szechenyi Jolan draws her support from the<br /> moderates, but she has no clear agenda regarding Gehenna .<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hand remains officially neutral on the candidates at<br /> present, waiting to see if one appears to be gaining strength and<br /> a clear majority among the consistory ; it is better to wait and<br /> back the winner than make a decision too early and be wrong .<br /> <b>The other option, should none of the three appear to hold a<br /> clear lead, and to prevent a crippling fourth Civil War, would<br /> be to carry out a Praetorian coup -pick a strong candidate,<br /> and install that candidate by force, using whatever means<br /> necessary to quell protests from the consistory or any surviving<br /> rivals. This would leave the new regent very much in the<br /> Hand's debt, though whether that might also backfire on them<br /> in other ways must also be taken into consideration . Until<br /> then, the Hand will do what it has done successfully for<br /> centuries- apparently nothing </b>. </div> </div> </div><br /> It will be just as before: The concistory will vote the candidate that the Seraphim will deem worth.<br /> And since now the only true Seraphim is Ajav this means that the concistory will vote whatever candidate Ajav-Khan will choose.<br /> <br /> At the moment we can pretty much say that Ajav-Khan is the de facto leader of the entire sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-20-2016, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:51:10-07:00","id":972824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972588#post972588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, I think pretty much the same thing any time I read your gibberish.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So am I <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You perfectly described my feeling about you. Sorry if I'm not very good at the English <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972588#post972588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There we go, sense at last! Still not sure how it relates to the original point, but let me take a crack at it. You already touched upon their rejection of Antediluvian mythology, the weaknesses of which are more a product of not being adequately explored in the text. As an extension of that Elder and Antediluvian cults are present beneath the surface of the sect, as are Infernalists and secret Path followers, any of which if exposed would threaten the Camarilla's gilded edifice and compromise what little ideology they profess to have. Somehow I don't think that's what you're looking for though. The Camarilla doesn't really have skeletons in the closet because their skeletons are on the living room couch. You only put them in the closet if you actually have a reason to hide them. The Camarilla only maintains the barest pretense of being a morally upright organization, their foundations are built on power and realpolitik. The only secret that would really shake those foundations is if it turned out they really had no power at all. Certainly the Antediluvian-denial is related to that, but in the end the Camarilla's pyramid scheme nature makes their power and strength (while not at all monolithic) a self-fulfilling prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? Thus the Sabbat, the Inconnu, the Black Hand, the Kuei-jin, the Werecreatures, the Mages or the Pentex secretly pulling strings behind back of the Camarilla, at least partially? Then I will admit Cam is not pristine nor immaculate as an institution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:02:11-07:00","id":972827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971380-special-projects-division-and-the-pentex-connection?p=972824#post972824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So am I <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You perfectly described my feeling about you. Sorry if I'm not very good at the English <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So what? Thus the Sabbat, the Inconnu, the Black Hand, the Kuei-jin, the Werecreatures or the Pentex secretly pulling strings of the Camarilla, at least partially? Then I will admit Cam is not pristine nor immaculate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing that I retract my statement and apologize for my tone. However the way your posts come off in English tend to give a very abrasive impression.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to be able to give you an answer that meets with your criteria. I still don't really see why it's a problem, or why how that makes the Cam &quot;pristine,&quot; but we're obviously not going to come to terms on it so I'm going to say we should probably just drop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}